 // Tunable per-material parameters:
 //   vertexParm 0   time, tint color rgb (multiplies the colormap - yzw)
 //   vertexParm 1   screenDistortMagnitude, flowStrength, tiling, gloss
+//   vertexParm 2   tintStrength (x) - how much the colormap tints the
+//                  refracted scene, 0 = fully clear, 1 = full strength.
+//                  How high this should be depends entirely on how dark/
+//                  opaque your source colormap texture already is - a
+//                  faint, barely-there colormap (texture packs that offer
+//                  several intensity variants, like a set numbered
+//                  5/10/20/30/40, often use the lowest number for this)
+//                  wants a LOW tintStrength here, or the shader can still
+//                  amplify it into a much stronger tint than the source
+//                  texture implies. Start low (0.1-0.2) and raise it if
+//                  the water reads as too weak/invisible.
 textures/liquid/mod_flowwater_example
